    "code": "def solution():\n    # Define variables name and value\n    stock_price = 120.0\n    strike_price = 130.0\n    risk_free_rate = 0.02\n    time_to_expiration = 1.0\n    volatility = 0.35\n\n    # Do math calculation to get the answer\n    from math import log, sqrt, exp, erf\n\n    def standard_normal_cdf(x):\n        return 0.5 * (1 + erf(x / sqrt(2)))\n\n    d1 = (\n        log(stock_price / strike_price)\n        + (risk_free_rate + 0.5 * volatility ** 2) * time_to_expiration\n    ) / (volatility * sqrt(time_to_expiration))\n\n    d2 = d1 - volatility * sqrt(time_to_expiration)\n\n    call_price = (\n        stock_price * standard_normal_cdf(d1)\n        - strike_price\n        * exp(-risk_free_rate * time_to_expiration)\n        * standard_normal_cdf(d2)\n    )\n\n    # return answer\n    return round(call_price, 2)\n"
